permissions:
  default: ask
jinx_name: shell-guide
skill_name: shell-guide
description: "Reference guide for the npcsh shell: core commands, modes, dispatch, team sync, and startup."
inputs:
- section: all
steps:
  - engine: skill
    skill_name: shell-guide
    skill_description: Reference guide for the npcsh shell.
    sections:
      what-is-npcsh: |
        `npcsh` is the main NPC OS shell: a Rust REPL built on `npcrs` that connects to an `npcpy.serve` backend.
        It loads a team, runs an interactive prompt, dispatches commands, and manages conversation history.

      modes: |
        - `/agent`: full agent mode — tools, bash, LLM. Plain non-command text goes to the LLM; recognized bash commands run locally.
        - `/chat`: LLM-only, no tools.
        - `/cmd`: bash first, LLM fallback if the input is not a runnable command.
        Switch modes with the slash commands or bare `agent`, `chat`, `cmd` aliases.

      core-commands: |
        Core commands always start with `/`:
        - Modes: `/agent`, `/chat`, `/cmd`
        - Terminal UIs: `/ctx`, `/git`, `/jinxes`, `/kg`, `/loop`, `/loops`, `/memories`, `/model`, `/ps`, `/stats`, `/team`
        - System / Config: `/clear`, `/config`, `/flush`, `/history`, `/reattach`
        - System Commands: `/init`, `/reload`, `/sync`, `/update`, `/verbose`
        - Info: `/exit`, `/help`, `/quit`, `/tutorial`
        Run `/help` in the shell to see the live list.

      jinx-invocation: |
        Jinxes are invoked by name without a leading slash: `compress`, `file_search pattern=*.py`.
        Use `/jinxes` to browse the loaded catalog.
        Tab completion works for `@npcs`, `/commands`, jinx names, and file paths.

      npc-addressing: |
        `@npc` switches the active process to that NPC across registered teams.
        `@npc command` delegates a single command to the NPC without changing the active process.

      team-sync: |
        `/sync` downloads the latest release tarball and copies default team files into `~/.npcsh/npc_team`.
        It preserves the `usr/` directory and any user-defined keys in `npcsh.ctx`.
        On startup a hint is shown if the recorded `team_version` does not match `npcsh`.

      init-and-rc: |
        `/init --force` creates `~/.npcsh/`, `~/.npcsh/bin/`, and `~/.npcsh/npc_team/`.
        `~/.npcshrc` is sourced on startup; common vars: `NPCSH_CHAT_MODEL`, `NPCSH_CHAT_PROVIDER`, `NPCSH_DEFAULT_MODE`, `NPCSH_MEMORY`.

      one-shot-cli: |
        `npc "prompt" [-n NPC] [-m MODEL] [-pr PROVIDER]` runs a single command through the agent.
        `npc <file.jinx> [args...]` executes a jinx file directly.
        `npc <file.npc> [command]` runs an NPC file.
        `npc init [dir]` initializes a new team directory.

      history-and-state: |
        Conversation history is stored in `~/npcsh_history.db` (SQLite).
        `/history` shows the current conversation; `/flush N` removes the last N messages.
        `/reattach [path|all]` lets you resume prior conversations from the database.

      startup-flow: |
        1. `npcsh` starts, loads `~/.npcshrc`, ensures the memory pref.
        2. Resolves the team directory (`~/.npcsh/npc_team` by default).
        3. Ensures the `npcpy.serve` backend is running.
        4. Boots the kernel, loads the team, and enters the REPL.
        5. Prints a sync hint if the default team files are out of date.

      customization: |
        Users can add jinxes to `jinxes/usr/` and custom context keys to `npcsh.ctx`.
        Both survive `/sync` updates. Framework jinxes live in `jinxes/lib/core/`, `jinxes/lib/search/`, and `jinxes/skills/`.
    scripts_json: '[]'
    references_json: '[]'
    assets_json: '[]'
    section: '{{section}}'
